"""PLAN §5 P8 gate tests (dltrain.gpu_gate). CPU-only, no network, no real nvidia-smi or systemctl call, CUDA never touched.

Every source is a fixture snapshot written under $TMPDIR (required; a /tmp TMPDIR is refused, and nothing is cleaned up):
queue-status.json, cpu-admission.json, nvidia-smi CSV output, /proc/locks text and systemctl output. Lock and unit
injections use a lane-owned dummy lock file and the lane-owned glob `jopedime-dltrain-p8test-gpu-*`; the real TabPFN lock and
the jopedime-incoming-* namespace are never used. Two tests read the real /proc/locks after taking a lock on the lane-owned
dummy file, and one starts a CPU-only child process to show the watchdog's default hard exit (os._exit(75)).
"""
